stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    state "active" as active
    state "checked_out" as checked_out
    state "timed_out" as timed_out
    state "manual_closed" as manual_closed

    [*] --> active: scanner check-in [device, QR, membership, no active session] / create session and check_in event
    active --> checked_out: scanner check-out [valid device and QR] / set closed_at and check_out event
    active --> timed_out: Celery every 5 minutes [checked_in_at <= cutoff] / set closed_at and timeout event
    active --> manual_closed: staff close [active row and reason] / set actor, reason, audit and event
    checked_out --> [*]
    timed_out --> [*]
    manual_closed --> [*]

    note bottom of active
        PostgreSQL partial unique index allows at most one active session per user.
        Row locks and one transaction protect closure; occupancy is then reconciled.
    end note
